{"name":"Snowbell","hex":"#bed0da","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"snowbell","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any member of the genus Soldanella of flowering plants native to European mountains, typically with a basal rosette of simple, orbicular leaves and white to violet flowers.","Any of certain styraxes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snowbell"}],"entries":[{"title":"Soldanella","blocks":[{"text":"The genus Soldanella, commonly known in English as snowbell, includes about 15 species of flowering plants native to European mountains, from the Pyrenees, the Apennines, the Alps, the Carpathians and the Balkans. They grow in woods, damp pastures and rocky landscapes from 500–3,000 m (1,600–9,800 ft) above sea level, often in hollows which hold snow into late spring and early summer. The name Soldanella means \"little coins\" in Italian."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Soldanella_alpina.jpg/330px-Soldanella_alpina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soldanella","wikidata":"Q158203"},{"title":"Styrax","blocks":[{"text":"Styrax is a genus of about 130 species of large shrubs or small trees in the family Styracaceae, mostly native to warm temperate to tropical regions of the Northern Hemisphere, with the majority in eastern and southeastern Asia, but also crossing the equator in South America. The resin obtained from the tree is called benzoin or storax, often used as a vanilla-like component in perfumery."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Styrax_platanifolius.jpg/330px-Styrax_platanifolius.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Styrax","wikidata":"Q525062"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Styrax_officinalis.jpg/500px-Styrax_officinalis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Styrax_officinalis.jpg/1280px-Styrax_officinalis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Styrax_officinalis.jpg/500px-Styrax_officinalis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Styrax officinalis resin was mainly used in antiquity","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStyrax_officinalis.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Styrax_benzoin_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-133.jpg/330px-Styrax_benzoin_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-133.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Styrax_benzoin_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-133.jpg/330px-Styrax_benzoin_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-133.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gum benjamin (Styrax benzoin) parts drawing.Franz Eugen Köhler: Köhler's Medizinal-Pflanzen in naturgetreuen Abbildungen, etc. (1887)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStyrax_benzoin_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-133.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Styrax_japonica1.JPG/500px-Styrax_japonica1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Styrax_japonica1.JPG/1280px-Styrax_japonica1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Styrax_japonica1.JPG/500px-Styrax_japonica1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Early summer blossoms of Styrax japonicus","link":"https://en.wikipedi